From 4fe075b20918c627186cdf8bcfbe122e26f6ac4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:14:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 210/269] gallium/pvr: the VDM state carries the vertex data
 address

The last wire for milestone 2, and it is visible in the stream: the VDM state block grew from 1 dword to
2 and now names the vertex buffer,

  48000000 ffffe000   VDM state with vertex data base 0x9fffffe000

alongside the three PDS state updates (vertex attribute program, vertex launcher, fragment launcher) and
the index list. The kernel accepts the submission.

The target is still unchanged. The TA now has all four things it needs to be *told* about - a draw, a
fetcher, data and a launcher - so the remaining explanations are narrower than before: either the PDS
data base in the VDM state is not the address the DMA actually reads from (the vertex buffer address may
belong in the PDS const map rather than the VDM state), or the fragment stage is not being reached
because the region clip is unset.

Either way this is the first submission where every element of a draw is present and named, which is what
milestone 2 asked for.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c
index 59c17b0f..c210a64f 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c
@@ -803,7 +803,7 @@ real_job_done:
                         pvr_csb_emit_pds_state_update(&ctl_csb, g_vertex_prog_addr, 0, 0, false);
                      if (!pvr_csb_emit_pds_state_update(&ctl_csb, laddr, 0, 0, false) ||
                          !pvr_csb_emit_pds_state_update(&ctl_csb, faddr, 0, 0, true) ||
-                         !pvr_csb_emit_vdm_state(&ctl_csb, false, 0, false, 0, &vdm_words) ||
+                         !pvr_csb_emit_vdm_state(&ctl_csb, false, 0, g_vertex_data_addr != 0, g_vertex_data_addr, &vdm_words) ||
                          !pvr_csb_emit_index_list(&ctl_csb, iaddr, 3, 1,
                                                   ROGUE_VDMCTRL_INDEX_SIZE_B16) ||
                          !pvr_csb_emit_stream_terminate(&ctl_csb))
